430 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 402 0 R
/E (The Digital RPM Meter Using Arduino is an efficient and accurate electronic system designed to measure the rotational speed of motors and rotating objects in terms of Revolutions Per Minute \(RPM\). The project is based on an Arduino Nano microcontroller, which acts as the central processing unit of the system. An IR sensor module is used to detect the rotation of the shaft or rotating object by sensing the reflection of infrared light from a reflective strip attached to the rotating surface. Each time the reflective strip passes in front of the sensor, a pulse signal is generated and sent to the Arduino.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
431 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 402 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
432 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 402 0 R
/E (An LED indicator is also included in the circuit to indicate pulse detection and proper system operation. The resistor is used for current limiting and protection of the LED. The I2C module simplifies LCD interfacing by reducing wiring complexity and minimizing the number of Arduino pins required.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
433 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 402 0 R
/E (The system provides high accuracy, fast response time, compact design, low power consumption, and reliable performance. The project demonstrates the practical implementation of sensors, embedded systems, microcontroller programming, and digital measurement techniques. It is highly useful in industrial automation, robotics, motor speed monitoring, laboratory experiments, and educational applications where accurate rotational speed measurement is required.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
