>>
endobj
714 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 410 0 R
/E (The IR transmitter continuously emits infrared light toward the rotating object. A reflective strip is attached to the rotating surface. Whenever the strip passes in front of the sensor, the infrared light reflects back to the receiver. The receiver detects this reflected light and generates a pulse signal.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [30]
>>
endobj
715 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 410 0 R
/E (In this project, each pulse represents one complete rotation. These pulse signals are sent to the Arduino Nano, which counts the pulses and calculates the RPM value. The calculated RPM is then displayed on the LCD display.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [31]
>>
endobj
