/P 414 0 R
/E (Pulse detection is the main process used to measure RPM in this project. The IR sensor continuously monitors the rotating fan blade or reflective strip attached to the motor shaft. The sensor contains an IR transmitter and IR receiver. The IR transmitter emits infrared light toward the rotating object. Whenever the reflective strip passes in front of the sensor, the infrared light reflects back to the receiver. The receiver detects this reflected light and generates a digital pulse signal. These pulses are sent to the Arduino Nano for RPM calculation.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
