1131 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 421 0 R
/E (The IR \(Infrared\) Sensor Module is used in the Digital RPM Meter project to detect the rotation of the motor fan and generate pulse signals for RPM calculation. It works on the principle of infrared light reflection and non-contact object detection.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [24]
>>
endobj
1132 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 421 0 R
/E (The sensor module mainly contains an IR transmitter \(IR LED\), IR receiver \(photodiode\), comparator circuit, sensitivity adjustment potentiometer, and indicator LED. The IR transmitter continuously emits infrared rays toward the rotating fan blade or reflective strip. Whenever the reflective surface passes in front of the sensor, the infrared light reflects back to the receiver section.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [25]
>>
endobj
1133 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 421 0 R
